slides.content:
1. Place an `<a>` as the first child of `<body>`.
2. Link it to the `id` of your `<main>` content.
3. Style it to be off‑screen until focused (using absolute positioning, not `display:none`).

Example:
```html
<a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>
```

```css
.skip-link {
  position: absolute;
  top: -40px;
  left: 0;
  background: #000;
  color: #fff;
  padding: 8px;
  z-index: 100;
}
.skip-link:focus {
  top: 0;
}
```
